in return for which I undertook to procure the requisite approbation of Your Royal Majesty's War and Domains Chamber to this contract.

Upon the ground of this contract the estate itself was now handed over to the said hereditary lessees naturaliter, though without any particular proceedings of delivery of possession, and the area of 3338. Morgen 14. rods Magdeburg measure, which had previously been exactly surveyed and revised by three sworn surveyors, Winitzki, Chwalowski and Cabanis, was assigned to them. After they had in this manner been placed in the full natural possession, they sub-let in hereditary sub-lease and dismembered a great part of the estate to the sub-lessees named in the annexed specification (B), and out of these monies, already levied contrary to the contract and payable directly to myself, they paid me the first half of the entry money with 10000 rthll:, and they also discharged successively the first year's lease rent. With the second half of the entry money, however, they remained in arrear, and in the second year they paid neither the hereditary lease rent nor the sovereign dues, which were thereupon levied from myself by execution by Your Royal Majesty's War and Domains Chamber to the amount of 431 Rthl;

